  "_skill_md": "---\nname: kalshi\ndescription: Internal API for kalshi\nmetadata:\n  author: unbrowse\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  baseUrl: \"https://api.elections.kalshi.com\"\n  authMethod: \"Unknown (may need login)\"\n  endpointCount: 20\n  apiType: \"internal\"\n  category: \"web-app\"\n---\n\n# Kalshi API\n\n> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.\n\n## Documentation Index\n- `SKILL.md` (this file)\n- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)\n- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)\n- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)\n\n## Authentication\nUnknown (may need login) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.\n\n### Providing credentials\n- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).\n- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.\n- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### Auth Flow (3)\n- `GET /markets/{marketId}/{kxbtc15mId}/{marketToken}` — Get market data for trading (requires authentication)\n- `GET /product-info/{product-infoToken}` — Get product information (requires authentication)\n- `GET /v1/series/{seryId}/events/{eventToken}` — Get event data for a series (requires authentication)\n\n### Data Read (10)\n- `GET /{id}` — Retrieve data by ID\n- `GET /category/{categoryId}` — Get details for a specific category\n- `GET /category/sports/all-sports` — Get a list of all sports categories\n- `GET /external/crypto/{cryptoId}` — Get crypto data from an external source\n- `GET /ideas/feed` — Get a feed of ideas\n- `GET /v1/{v1Id}` — Retrieve data from a v1 endpoint\n- `GET /v1/exchange/status` — Check the exchange status\n- `GET /v1/markets/order_books` — Get order book data for markets\n- `GET /v1/series/{seryId}/markets/{marketId}/forecast_history` — Get historical forecast data for a market\n- `GET /v1/social/{socialId}` — Retrieve social data\n\n### Data Write (4)\n- `POST /{id}` — Post data to an endpoint\n- `POST /tag/v1/event/pageview` — Report a page view event\n- `POST /v1/{v1Id}` — Post data to a v1 endpoint\n- `POST /v2/client_infos` — Submit client information\n\n### Search (1)\n- `GET /v1/search/{searchId}` — Search for content\n\n### Config (2)\n- `GET /tag/v1/configs/kalshi.json` — Retrieve Kalshi configuration settings\n- `GET /v1/config/{configId}` — Retrieve configuration data\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow\n- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).\n- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.\n- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode=\"backend\"`.\n\nExample:\n```text\nunbrowse_replay { service: \"kalshi\", executionMode: \"backend\", endpoint: \"GET /{id}\" }\n```\n\nHere's a Quick Start guide to using the Kalshi API:\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Retrieving market data for trading (requires authentication)\nasync function getMarketData(marketId: string, kxbtc15mId: string, marketToken: string) {\n  try {\n    const marketData = await client.getMarketsMarketIdKxbtc15mIdMarketToken({ marketId, kxbtc15mId, marketToken });\n    console.log(\"Market Data:\", marketData);\n    return marketData;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error fetching market data:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Posting client information\nasync function submitClientInfo(clientInfo: any) { // Replace 'any' with a more specific type if available\n  try {\n    const response = await client.postV2ClientInfos(clientInfo);\n    console.log(\"Client Info Submission Response:\", response);\n    return response;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error submitting client info:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n**Type:** Reverse-engineered internal API (unofficial)\n**Auth:** Unknown (may need login)\n**Base URL:** `https://api.elections.kalshi.com`\n**Captured Auth:** 3 auth headers, 44 session cookies\n\n## About This Skill\n\nThis skill provides access to Kalshi's internal API — the hidden endpoints that power their web/mobile app.\nThese are NOT official public APIs. They were captured by observing network traffic while using the site.\n\n**Important:**\n- Auth tokens in `auth.json` may expire — re-capture if you get 401 errors\n- Internal APIs can change without notice — endpoints may break\n- Rate limits are unknown — be conservative with request frequency\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Access Kalshi data without official API access\n- Automate actions on api.elections.kalshi.com (faster than browser automation)\n- Call the same endpoints the Kalshi frontend uses\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\nimport { KalshiClient } from \"./scripts/api.ts\";\n\n// Load captured auth from auth.json\nconst client = await KalshiClient.fromAuthFile(\"auth.json\");\n\n// Make requests to internal endpoints\nconst result = await client.get(\"/endpoint\");\n```\n\n## Captured Authentication\n\nThe `auth.json` file contains credentials extracted from browser traffic:\n- **Auth headers:** 3 (sec-fetch-storage-access, access-control-allow-headers, access-control-allow-origin)\n- **Session cookies:** 44\n\nIf auth expires, re-run `unbrowse_login` or `unbrowse_capture` to refresh tokens.\n\n## Internal Endpoints (62)\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  const data = await client.get(\"/resource\");\n} catch (err) {\n  if (err.message.includes(\"401\")) {\n    // Auth expired — need to re-capture\n    console.error(\"Auth expired, re-run unbrowse_login\");\n  } else {\n    console.error(\"API error:\", err.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee [REFERENCE.md](references/REFERENCE.md) for detailed endpoint documentation.\n"
